# PR Diff Truncated

Original size: 80434 characters.
Kept: first 7800 and last 4200 characters.

The full diff is available in the checked-out PR branch. Use `git diff` or CodeGraph for focused source navigation instead of relying only on this file.

```diff
diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index a66fe100f0..8151372226 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -13,7 +13,31 @@ block a release again.

 ## Unreleased

-- feat(gh-209): two-tier compaction engine вЂ” the mid-turn relief paths
+- feat(2117): console logging dial — `lib/src/logging/` levels
+  (`off < error < warn < info < debug < trace`), categories
+  (`keys/lifecycle/tool/provider/compaction/messaging`), and the
+  `{time} {elapsed} {sid} {level} {cat} {msg}` line pattern with
+  `logging.timeFormat`, rendered only when `logging.format` is set (the
+  current shapes stay otherwise). The INTERACTIVE console filters at the
+  resolved level (default `warn`); `fa.log` filters at its own level
+  (default `debug` — every existing diagnostic line still lands, now
+  with a level tag) and every rendered line on every sink passes the
+  redaction pipeline. Sources: `--log-level` flag > `FA_LOG_LEVEL` env >
+  project `.fah/config.yaml` `logging:` > user `~/.fah/config.yaml`
+  `logging:` > default; invalid levels fail loudly at boot;
+  `--debug-secrets`/`FA_DEBUG_KEYS` stay as the `keys=debug` alias
+  (a keys-category floor, never resurrecting an explicit `off`).
+  `/log <level>` switches the console sink live in the REPL. The
+  headless stdout contract is PINNED byte-identical: HEP/stream-json/
+  wire-serve/plain-run output never routes through the filter unless the
+  flag or the env makes the level explicit. The passive `info: agent
+  stalled` banner is the first reassigned noise class (it obeys the
+  dial — hidden at the interactive default, shown from `info` up); tool
+  start/finish diagnostics reassign to `debug`/`tool` (fa.log keeps
+  passing them at its `debug` default). Background-chatter and echo
+  reassignment follow in #2118's follow-up.
+
+- feat(gh-209): two-tier compaction engine — the mid-turn relief paths
   (the loop's over-window guard and the gh-1680 message-cap self-heal,
   CLI and Flutter app) now run ONLY the deterministic emergency tier
   (`EmergencyRelief`): re-anchor from the session projection, dedup
diff --git a/bin/fah_runapp.dart b/bin/fah_runapp.dart
index ce758d8552..46c4a61790 100644
--- a/bin/fah_runapp.dart
+++ b/bin/fah_runapp.dart
@@ -1031,6 +1031,26 @@ Future<void> _runApp(List<String> args) async {
   // one (same merge as the other project sections). Null = absent —
   // no spill hooks, byte-identical legacy boot.
   final spillsConfig = loadProjectSpillsConfig(cwd) ?? saved.spills;
+  // The console log dial (issue #2117): flag > env > project
+  // .fah/config.yaml `logging:` > user ~/.fah/config.yaml `logging:` >
+  // the `warn` interactive default. An invalid level is a LOUD boot
+  // failure, never a silent fallthrough. Headless stdout stays pinned:
+  // the resolved level filters the interactive console only (headless
+  // opts in solely via the flag/env — `consoleExplicit`).
+  final ResolvedLogSettings loggingSettings;
+  try {
+    loggingSettings = resolveLogSettings(
+      flagLevel: parsed.logLevel,
+      envLevel: Platform.environment['FA_LOG_LEVEL'],
+      project: loadProjectLoggingSection(cwd),
+      user: saved.logging,
+      debugKeys:
+          parsed.debugSecrets ||
+          isTruthyEnvValue(Platform.environment['FA_DEBUG_KEYS']),
+    );
+  } on ConfigException catch (error) {
+    _fail(error.message);
+  }
   // The projectContext budget (issue #1761): user-level `projectContext:`
   // section only — a global resource knob, not a repo-traveling one.
   final projectContextConfig = saved.projectContext;
@@ -1628,6 +1648,10 @@ Future<void> _runApp(List<String> args) async {
         // runner's $RUNNER_TEMP). Null keeps <cwd>/.fah/bash_jobs.
         jobLogDir: jobLogDirOverride(Platform.environment),
         spills: spillsConfig,
+        // The resolved console/file log dial (issue #2117): flag > env >
+        // project config > user config > defaults; headless stdout is
+        // only filtered when the flag/env made the level explicit.
+        logging: loggingSettings,
         // gh-1746: the opt-in sessions retention policy (user config);
         // null = the section is absent — no sweep, no note (AC1).
         sessionsRetention: saved.sessions,
